{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/190544-wishlist-for-the-demon-storyteller-s-guide","id":190544,"title":"Wishlist for the Demon Storyteller's Guide","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-07T11:34:40-07:00","id":190544,"title":"Wishlist for the Demon Storyteller's Guide","content":"I know some of these have already been announced/discussed, but I'm including them for completion.<br /> <br /> Advice on how to run the game in low tech historical eras, with medieval Byzantium as an example. (Maybe be unnecessary depending on what Dark Eras ends up covering.)<br /> More example Angels and advice on how and when to build them for combat. <br /> Additional support for pickup games, including sample Interlocks, and gameplay variants that includes players in the creation of interlocks. <br /> Variants on the Pact system that involve Demons having to implement something like an occult matrix to hold up their end of the bargain. <br /> Discussions on how to handle Cover, Pacts, and Ciphers in crossover groups. <br /> Expansion of Exiles and Qashmallim. For instance, should Integrators who become Exiles get to continue playing? Are there any potential goals they could have that would keep them in a Demon group, or are they by definition excluded?<br /> <br /> I'm just spitballing here, and I'm aware that some of these ideas probably won't work or are incompatible with the themes of the game. <br /> <br /> Does anyone else have any ideas for the ST Guide for Demon? Failing that, has anyone else built any mods or houserules they'd like to share?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T11:58:16-07:00","id":190602,"title":"","content":"I want Exiles and a thorough discussion of The Principle/qashmallim. Anything else is just gravy for me.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Advice for historical games would make me very happy indeed. I'm all but certain the Dark Era is gonna be Cold War.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 07-07-2014, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T12:25:21-07:00","id":190618,"title":"","content":"I really want some in-depth treatment of Angels, their Influences and Infrastructure, in addition to how Angels maintain &quot;covers&quot; and stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T13:57:57-07:00","id":190689,"title":"","content":"I don't need anything from Promethean.<br /> <br /> But definitely Exiles. I want an Exile Chapter that will blow my pants off.<br /> <br /> And Hell. I want Hell. I want a discussion about actually attaining it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T14:46:59-07:00","id":190763,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Looked back through the Kickstarter comments, and found a tantalizing one by Rose Bailey in response to a question about Lucifer. &quot;...<span style=\"color:#0F2105\">Some big name demons may be dealt with in the Storyteller's Guide. I've got a plan for Satan, for example. But since that book isn't at the outline stage yet, I can't tell you what will be in it for sure.&quot; </span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T15:09:16-07:00","id":190780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/190544-wishlist-for-the-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=190689#post190689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't need anything from Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Normally I hate crossover material, but I was one of the people who (wrongly) believed that this game was going to be about playing <i>qashmallim</i>. I'd be happy enough with just being incorrect, but their inclusion in the <i>Demon</i> core has had my interest piqued ever since. Someone, somewhere, said that the God-Machine is sometimes referred to as &quot;the Purpose,&quot; which provides a nice contrary to &quot;the Principle.&quot; The devs are doing something here, and I hope it's as satisfying as I've built it up to be in my head.<br /> <br /> <i>Demon</i> is a tech<b>gnostic</b> game, after all; exploring God-Machine as demiurge and Principle as true divinity would be fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T15:18:25-07:00","id":190792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/190544-wishlist-for-the-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=190780#post190780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Demon</i> is a tech<b>gnostic</b> game, after all; exploring God-Machine as demiurge and Principle as true divinity would be fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm largely content with the Principle occupying the same unclear position as the Machine, to be frank. It puts their degree of entanglement at a nice level of ambiguity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T15:30:25-07:00","id":190803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/190544-wishlist-for-the-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=190763#post190763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Looked back through the Kickstarter comments, and found a tantalizing one by Rose Bailey in response to a question about Lucifer. &quot;...<span style=\"color:#0F2105\">Some big name demons may be dealt with in the Storyteller's Guide. I've got a plan for Satan, for example. But since that book isn't at the outline stage yet, I can't tell you what will be in it for sure.&quot; </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A while ago I compiled all the info I could find on the possible content of ST Guide. Crossposting:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><ul><li>\u201cDeeper looks at the ongoing struggle to survive on the run from the God-Machine\u201d</li> <li>Chronicle examples</li> <li>Rule variants (<span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><u><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/silent-snow-not-so-secret-snow/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/silent-snow-not-so-secret-snow/</a></u></span>)</li> <li>Ciphers and Interlocks (<span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><u><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10068-the-cipher?p=10360#post10360\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...0360#post10360</a></u></span>)</li> <li>Info on Angels and Exiles (<span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><u><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11982-can-angels-be-nearly-as-complex-and-cool-as-demons?p=17470#post17470\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...7470#post17470</a></u></span>)<ul><li>Including new Numina (<span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><u><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/69948-infrastructure-condition-angels?p=74542#post74542\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...4542#post74542</a></u></span>)</li> </ul></li> <li>Big name Demons, such as Satan (<span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><u><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition/comments?cursor=5084744&amp;direction=asc\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects...&amp;direction=asc</a></u></span>)</li> <li>The Prisoner references; Sandbox envirnements created by the Deva Corporation to harvest demonic parts (<span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><u><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition/comments?cursor=5079618#comment-5079617\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects...omment-5079617</a></u></span>)</li> <li>Possibly urban legends Demons tell each other, including the Satan Signal (<span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><u><a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?705326-Demon-the-Descent-what-do-you-want-from-it-Part-3&amp;p=17378861#post17378861\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...1#post17378861</a></u></span>)</li> <li>Possibly in-depth look at Facilities? (Couldn\u2019t find a direct references but there was a mention here: <span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><u><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/62059-is-there-going-to-be-an-endgame-book-for-demon?p=62157#post62157\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...2157#post62157</a></u></span>)</li> <li>Possibly crossover rules (<span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><u><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition/comments?cursor=5243045#comment-5243044\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects...omment-5243044</a></u></span>)<ul><li>Including how the God-Machine related to the Principle, the Gentry and the Strix (<span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><u><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/DemonTheDescent/posts/219774381531259?stream_ref=5\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/DemonTheDes...9?stream_ref=5</a></u></span>)</li> </ul></li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","name":"genesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T15:31:40-07:00","id":190804,"title":"","content":"Antagonists, antagonists, antagonists. Not just angels (though <i>plenty</i> of them, thank you very much). any RPG thrives on interesting, varied, and dangerous challenges. Look at the acid-trip inspired rogues gallery of Werewolf and Mage. How do we keep Angels from becoming ho-hum Monster Of The Week, or sleepers from becoming Mook of the Week, how does a Story-Teller keep a player nervous, scared, and <i>guessing</i>? Angelic tactics for reacting to embeds and exploits would be welcome (see Extra Credits section on Counter Play)<br /> <br /> Genre conventions: Car chases in a world where drivers can warp reality, tradecraft when the opposition can warp reality, assassinating a world leaders who's on God's payroll. How do we translate Jason Bourne and George Smilely into the World of Darkness?<br /> <br /> Ciphers: a real hard look here please. Most of the Ciphers we've seen are more like fortune cookies then pieces of gnostic truth worth fighting for. For instant Ms. Cook of the premade characters has a cipher that just reinforces her existing world view; no change in character arc.<br /> <br /> Chronicle-building: How do story tellers put to together adventures, and how are they built into into a satisfying chronicle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T15:49:38-07:00","id":190815,"title":"","content":"Isn't The Principle/Qashmallim squarely in the Promethean gameline?<br /> <br /> However, +1 for crossover content, even though I can almost guarantee they will not devote much if any wordspace in a new gameline's nucleus of books.<br /> <br /> Since Hell seems to be the intended meta-purpose for 90% of the PCs, I would definitely want some more discussion on that. Ideas about what makes <b>a </b>Hell be <b>Hell</b>, why the God-Machine wouldn't be able to subsume it, etc. etc.<br /> <br /> For Demon games, I also don't quite <i>get</i> Exiles. Not only what they are, but what role they were intended to play in the narrative.<br /> <br /> And because I'm going to shamelessly steal as much as I can for non-Demon games, Angels when not in Murder/Death/Kill mode.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T16:00:10-07:00","id":190822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paddon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/190544-wishlist-for-the-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=190815#post190815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't The Principle/Qashmallim squarely in the Promethean gameline?<br /> <br /> However, +1 for crossover content, even though I can almost guarantee they will not devote much if any wordspace in a new gameline's nucleus of books.<br /> <br /> Since Hell seems to be the intended meta-purpose for 90% of the PCs, I would definitely want some more discussion on that. Ideas about what makes <b>a </b>Hell be <b>Hell</b>, why the God-Machine wouldn't be able to subsume it, etc. etc.<br /> <br /> For Demon games, I also don't quite <i>get</i> Exiles. Not only what they are, but what role they were intended to play in the narrative.<br /> <br /> And because I'm going to shamelessly steal as much as I can for non-Demon games, Angels when not in Murder/Death/Kill mode.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exiles sound like the Merovingian in the Matrix to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T17:15:58-07:00","id":190916,"title":"","content":"Mechanical expansion for angels, especially material related to them being in cover versus twilight versus an angelic form; I've patched together my own ideas but I don't have an editor or accomplices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T17:22:41-07:00","id":190917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paddon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/190544-wishlist-for-the-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=190815#post190815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Demon games, I also don't quite <i>get</i> Exiles. Not only what they are, but what role they were intended to play in the narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truefacs - they're basically Descent's version of Earthbound. The big, old, powerful guys who aren't on your side but aren't on the opposition's side either.<br /> <br /> The Infrastructure and Agencies chapter of the player's guide has an Exile in its chapter fiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T17:37:47-07:00","id":190943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/190544-wishlist-for-the-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=190780#post190780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Normally I hate crossover material, but I was one of the people who (wrongly) believed that this game was going to be about playing <i>qashmallim</i>. I'd be happy enough with just being incorrect, but their inclusion in the <i>Demon</i> core has had my interest piqued ever since. Someone, somewhere, said that the God-Machine is sometimes referred to as &quot;the Purpose,&quot; which provides a nice contrary to &quot;the Principle.&quot; The devs are doing something here, and I hope it's as satisfying as I've built it up to be in my head.<br /> <br /> <i>Demon</i> is a tech<b>gnostic</b> game, after all; exploring God-Machine as demiurge and Principle as true divinity would be fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's that true divinity part that makes me go all squinty with my eyes.<br /> <br /> That aside, I don't want Demon telling me about a primarily Promethean concept. Allusions are fun and all, but forcing greater associations is...not kosher.<br /> <br /> Also, how the hell did you ever get the idea this game'd ever be about playing qashmallim?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T17:56:40-07:00","id":190976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paddon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/190544-wishlist-for-the-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=190815#post190815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> For Demon games, I also don't quite <i>get</i> Exiles. Not only what they are, but what role they were intended to play in the narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAngels who popped into reality with no connection to the God-Machine. They provide a nice foil to the Unchained, as sort of your weird cousins; Angels are loyal, you are not loyal, Exiles never had a choice in the matter. They might well resent Demons, as you chose your fate while they got screwed over through no fault of their own. I'm real excited for more on them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/190544-wishlist-for-the-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=190943#post190943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's that true divinity part that makes me go all squinty with my eyes.<br /> <br /> That aside, I don't want Demon telling me about a primarily Promethean concept. Allusions are fun and all, but forcing greater associations is...not kosher.<br /> <br /> Also, how the hell did you ever get the idea this game'd ever be about playing qashmallim?</div> </div> </div> </div>True divinity in gnostic language, not as any sort of &quot;real God&quot; for the World of Darkness. The God-Machine as a flawed imitation of the Principle, essentially.<br /> <br /> As for how I thought that, blame whichever book it was that discussed the Divine Fire. One of the options for &quot;what is the Principle?&quot; literally defined it as &quot;a God-Machine.&quot; That was the same book that had Ruby and Mister Gold, who I think have been confirmed to be <i>Descent</i> Demons, but referred to them as <i>qashmallim</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T22:18:57-07:00","id":192008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/190544-wishlist-for-the-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=190917#post190917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Truefacs - they're basically Descent's version of Earthbound. The big, old, powerful guys who aren't on your side but aren't on the opposition's side either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been only somewhat interested in more info about Exiles, mostly just to know more of the setting, but now I can't wait to know more about them.<br /> <br /> What I would want form the ST guide is:<br /> - More on the Exiles, especially now that they are hinted to be Earthbound equivalents.<br /> - More on Hell, what is it, how to achieve it etc,<br /> - Cipher, basically just something that would give me anything more than the fortune cookie sentence at the end. In the end players will end up deciphering their Ciphers for two things, Interlocks and to get closer to Hell. The first is self-explanatory, more power and personal unique powers at that, the second sounds reasonable but has no teeth currently since we have literally nothing on Hell and because I at least have found the so called end goal for the Cipher to be rather anti-climatic. Like said it currently seems to be a fortune cookie line that the ST hopes is something that is somehow revelationary for the character.<br /> - More on Angels<br /> - More on Infrastructure and how demons may manipulate it or even create it for themselves, then again I suspect this might be what makes the Exiles powerful especially if they are powerful in anything remotely Earthbound sense.<br /> <br /> Personally I don't feel much of a need to devote word count to historical games in the ST guide, especially since I at least see humanity's technological advancements largely irrelevant to Demons/G-M/Angels except that more advanced the technology humans use the easier it becomes for the G-M and it's agents to monitor and control them through it. No need for Angelic revelations anymore when you can make sure the information you want to distribute get's distributed through a few well placed words on the net.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T14:19:11-07:00","id":192751,"title":"","content":"Here's my big three: * Hell - More about the search, and how it works. Preferably the &quot;official&quot; version of Hell too, so we can decide how to fit it in to our chronicles, or not to. * Cyphers - I'd like to see a huge section devoted to example builds, example interlocks, and even unique situations that may arise in the search. Possibly even mechanical bonus recommendations for the final truth learned. * Infrastructure - Location location location. The information in the core book isn't bad, but it needs more fleshing out. More systems, more examples, and more more more. The setting really helps set the mood, and infrastructures make great locations for adventures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1755-dalarpguy","name":"dalarpguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T15:57:47-07:00","id":192844,"title":"","content":"To expand on one of the items I mentioned, I find myself a little uncomfortable with the notion of choosing Keys and designing Interlocks for players, since it's an odd subversion of the role of the Storyteller. Generally the ST makes the NPCs (and sometimes their powers), sets up the scenes, and works with the players to build a story. The players design their characters and choose powers they think are thematic, fun, or optimally designed for their intended character concept. I feel almost like assigning powers interferes with allowing the players to design their characters. <br /> <br /> Alternate systems for ciphers that put more power in the hands of the players might be worth having since it decentralizes the role of the ST and is more conducive to pickup games. Sample lists of Interlocks could also speed up game prep or at least provide inspiration for building ciphers. For instance, I know that when I decide to design ciphers, I'll be looking at the 12 or so Interlocks provided in the Ready Made Character Pack.<br /> <br /> All that said, subverting typical expectations for player/ST roles is often a good thing, so regardless of what appears in any sourcebook, I'm going to dive right in and try to make the best ciphers I can for the games I plan to run in the near future. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T19:43:07-07:00","id":193010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/190544-wishlist-for-the-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=192844#post192844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To expand on one of the items I mentioned, I find myself a little uncomfortable with the notion of choosing Keys and designing Interlocks for players, since it's an odd subversion of the role of the Storyteller. Generally the ST makes the NPCs (and sometimes their powers), sets up the scenes, and works with the players to build a story. The players design their characters and choose powers they think are thematic, fun, or optimally designed for their intended character concept. I feel almost like assigning powers interferes with allowing the players to design their characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think - and don't quote me on this as I didn't write on the core book (I just playtested the thing) - that the idea is to discuss the journey with the player. You don't just say &quot;Hey, what's your starting Embed?&quot; and go from there. It's a discussion about the demon's view of Hell, of the God-Machine, of her place in the world, and so on. It's not just the Storyteller deciding the character's journey. It's a communication between player and ST - although one might not want to go too far down that road because that'll tip off the player as to the other Keys in the Cipher.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alternate systems for ciphers that put more power in the hands of the players might be worth having since it decentralizes the role of the ST and is more conducive to pickup games. Sample lists of Interlocks could also speed up game prep or at least provide inspiration for building ciphers. For instance, I know that when I decide to design ciphers, I'll be looking at the 12 or so Interlocks provided in the Ready Made Character Pack. </div> </div> </div>Seriously, thank you for that. It was the first thing I did for Onyx Path, so having someone say they'll use it for inspiration (or what-have-you) for their own games is very satisfying. Although, for Cascading Collapse, I'm not entirely certain it conveys my intent 100%, but I suppose those things happen. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All that said, subverting typical expectations for player/ST roles is often a good thing, so regardless of what appears in any sourcebook, I'm going to dive right in and try to make the best ciphers I can for the games I plan to run in the near future. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>So far, I've found that talking to the players about where they see their character going, and what sort of story arc they want/expect goes a long way toward helping with that. For the <b>Ready Made Characters</b>, I obviously cheated a bit because everything was my own creation, but communication is key when it comes to making Ciphers for your players. At least in my experience so far.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T02:31:28-07:00","id":193315,"title":"","content":"1. Angels! Detailed explanation/guidance with plenty of *examples* of how to use the blue book ephemeral rules for Angels. <br /> (i) *Guidance* for when the ST should keep track of an angel's Essence and various ephemeral conditions and when the ST should feel more free-form in handwaving interactions with Angels. <br /> (ii) *Guidance* when to use Influences, when to use Manifestations and when to use Numina. <br /> (iii) Confirmation or refutation of the fact that Embeds are Numina and, if confirmed, how to square Essence costs for Numina with the free nature of Embeds.<br /> (iv) Generally, guidance on how to make interactions between Angels and Demons interesting, while keeping the improvisation elements of Angelic powers manageable<br /> I am aware, from the other thread that turned nasty, that a lot of posters on these boards do not consider this to be worthy of attention. But for me, and at least some others, clarification of this would be of great value.<br /> <br /> 2. More guidance on compromise rolls and how often to make players roll them to create a fluid and organic gaming experience. In particular, thoughts on the Partial Transformation beat-generator effect.<br /> <br /> 3. Cipher. And more specifically more on the Final Truth. Also the possibility of starting a new Cipher once the first one is complete. <br /> <br /> 4. Facilities and their interaction with Primum. And generally more guidance on changing Primum.<br /> <br /> 5.Hell<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","name":"genesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T17:20:30-07:00","id":194130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/190544-wishlist-for-the-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=193010#post193010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think - and don't quote me on this as I didn't write on the core book (I just playtested the thing) - that the idea is to discuss the journey with the player. You don't just say &quot;Hey, what's your starting Embed?&quot; and go from there. It's a discussion about the demon's view of Hell, of the God-Machine, of her place in the world, and so on. It's not just the Storyteller deciding the character's journey. It's a communication between player and ST - although one might not want to go too far down that road because that'll tip off the player as to the other Keys in the Cipher.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good way to frame it. Much like STing isn't the ST telling it how it is, it's a form of collaborative storytelling.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/190544-wishlist-for-the-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=193010#post193010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, thank you for that. It was the first thing I did for Onyx Path, so having someone say they'll use it for inspiration (or what-have-you) for their own games is very satisfying. Although, for Cascading Collapse, I'm not entirely certain it conveys my intent 100%, but I suppose those things happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole character pack was great. It felt like a whole third adventure, after the quickstart, and &quot;How an Angel Dies.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/190544-wishlist-for-the-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=193010#post193010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far, I've found that talking to the players about where they see their character going, and what sort of story arc they want/expect goes a long way toward helping with that. For the <b>Ready Made Characters</b>, I obviously cheated a bit because everything was my own creation, but communication is key when it comes to making Ciphers for your players. At least in my experience so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll keep that in mind. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T02:04:58-07:00","id":194451,"title":"","content":"I'd really like to see something on Qashmallim, yeah. I think Matt or Rose mentioned their preference was to do them up the same way Mage's Arcadia is presented in that one Changeling supplement (Rites of Spring?). Lots of options, no definitive answers.<br /> <br /> And yes, more on Exiles and Angels.<br /> <br /> Maybe something on styles of play? The spy genre can be really varied. I can see Demon being played in a mode anywhere between John Carre and Ian Flemming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T05:42:05-07:00","id":194582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/190544-wishlist-for-the-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=194451#post194451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd really like to see something on Qashmallim, yeah. I think Matt or Rose mentioned their preference was to do them up the same way Mage's Arcadia is presented in that one Changeling supplement (Rites of Spring?). Lots of options, no definitive answers.<br /> <br /> And yes, more on Exiles and Angels.<br /> <br /> Maybe something on styles of play? The spy genre can be really varied. I can see Demon being played in a mode anywhere between John Carre and Ian Flemming.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm happy to double down on those ideas. Prommie isn't likely to get an update and it doesn't exactly explain Qashmallim anyway...<br /> <br /> Some advice on 'localizing' the God-Machine to different places and time periods would be nice too, along with some ideas on Hell.<br /> <br /> But the main things that I think <i><b>need</b></i> to be in the Storyteller's Guide are as follows:<ul><li>Exiles</li> <li>Angels</li> <li>Ciphers</li> <li>Infrastructure/Facilities</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T07:21:20-07:00","id":194617,"title":"","content":"I think we got plenty on Infrastructure in Flowers of Hell, but it might be good to have more example Occult Matrices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T22:31:35-07:00","id":195268,"title":"","content":"I'm double dipping but...<br /> <br /> Merits: Do you see the mind-bending merits the Forsaken are getting in Idigam Chronicles? Can we get some for Demon, stuff like City Walker? which is just plain weird (and awesome) but embodies the sort of themes that DtD embraces: kinship with City Environments, exploitation of occult knowledge, and dramatic failures causing wierdness. It's a human-only advantage, which I think is a damn shame.<br /> <br /> Demonify your City: How can we turn our home cities in G-M controlled nightmare zones? I look forward to telling my players that the schools their children attend are occult matrices and their places of work are G-M cults. If m players are able to get a decent nights sleep after playing with me I've failed as a storyteller.<br /> <br /> More on Agendas/incarnations: compared to Vampires, Mages and especially Forsaken, the impact of splats is pretty cosmetic: a condition, a beat, and some general roleplaying direction. Can we do more to distinguish one incarnation from the there?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/190544-wishlist-for-the-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=193010#post193010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seriously, thank you for that. It was the first thing I did for Onyx Path, so having someone say they'll use it for inspiration (or what-have-you) for their own games is very satisfying.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The characters were excellent, and I especially like Ms. Cook as an example of alien, somewhat sinister intelligence, trying to be human in disturbing ways. If Onyx path ever decides to update it, for heaven's sake, please put a sheet in for James Sherman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T14:12:36-07:00","id":195736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/190544-wishlist-for-the-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=194130#post194130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a good way to frame it. Much like STing isn't the ST telling it how it is, it's a form of collaborative storytelling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, exactly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The whole character pack was great. It felt like a whole third adventure, after the quickstart, and &quot;How an Angel Dies.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Again, thanks! And to keep this short so I'm not hijacking the thread - ratings and reviews on DriveThru help us all out a lot. (This is not a help *me* out thing - I don't personally get anything from it - it's just helpful for all of us who write this stuff. The more positive reviews/ratings there are (and of course, sales), the more stuff we get to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'll keep that in mind. Thanks! </div> </div> </div>You're quite welcome!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T14:15:39-07:00","id":195739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/190544-wishlist-for-the-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=195268#post195268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IThe characters were excellent, and I especially like Ms. Cook as an example of alien, somewhat sinister intelligence, trying to be human in disturbing ways. If Onyx path ever decides to update it, for heaven's sake, please put a sheet in for James Sherman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me double-check and see if it's cool, but I <i>might</i> be able to whip up a character sheet right quick for those who are keen on it. Obviously we didn't put one in there because he's not at all the focus (the characters are), and different ST's might want different things out of him. I don't know if I'd even use a sheet for him - I'd probably just wing any dice pools if necessary. But I'll check and if it's cool I'll do one up and post it.<br /> <br /> And now I'm going to stop derailing the thread, I swear.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T21:27:27-07:00","id":196013,"title":"","content":"I'm really interested in Seraphim and would like to see something on these powerful angels. Like, do they belong to a different Incarnation? How spectacular is it when they fall? <br /> An Allies and Antagonist section, things that can act as either for the God-machine and Demons.<br /> I'd rather not see new Embeds or exploits unless the former belong to a new group.<br /> It was suggested that some Demon's hunt for a 5th key, is there something to that?<br /> Hell; I'd like essays about it from the various writers and Dev's. Not hard and fast rules but opinion pieces. I don't think this book needs to be Imperial Mysteries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T04:58:20-07:00","id":196194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is in the corebook, they're not that powerful. Like angels, they're Rank 1-5 spirits with a ban and a bane, no listed ability to heal aggravated damage or inflict it, limited number of Numina, and dependent on acquiring Essence without Infrastructure in the Exiles' case. They'd have to be seriously beefed up to be what the Earthbound were in D:tF, the default antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Angels aren't like Demons who need to worry about where their next hit of aether is coming from, sacrifices from cultists can replenish their essence, and seeing as how demons can have cults I see absolutely no reason to think that an exile can't have a cult or two as well.<br /> <br /> Angels quickly gain higher stats than non ephemerals, exasperated by their ability to freely spend their essence to enhance their stats by rank plus 2.<br /> <br /> If push comes to shove, a rank three angel can spend 15 essence to enhance their stats across the board by 5, allowing stats of 13,13, and 14. So no matter how you put the stats that's an attack roll of at least 26, defense of at least 13, speed of at least 29, and at least 18 health levels.<br /> <br /> A fifth rank angel can have stats of 15 across the board, and with essence expenditure they can have 22 across the board, so 44 attack dice, defense 22, speed 33, and 27 health levels.<br /> <br /> Or they can go the other way and use influences, which is basically reality control that can be as versatile as mage arcana, at rank three an angel might be sporting up to 10 levels of influence, 16 levels for rank 5 angels, they just have to be in theme for the angel. Let's see, for example, there is an angel of time in GMC. So time 5, maybe movement 4 and death 4,as related concepts, and maybe space 3 considering the whole space/time thing.<br /> <br /> So in short, ephemerals are basically mages without paradox who often have superhuman stats to boot, if an ST can't figure out how to ruin a players day with that then they really aren't trying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T08:15:51-07:00","id":196792,"title":"","content":"To add to the general requests for things in the ST Guide -<br /> <br /> (Nothing new here really...)<br /> <br /> 1) Angels -<br /> <br /> Explaining (or reexplainning) the mechanically elements of angels (e.g. exactly how the many, many rules that apply to them between the GMC (twilight form as default? loosing essence every hour outside infrastructure) core and Demon interact (can Angel's have Numina that are basically Embed effects? do/can they have &quot;form abilities&quot; like Demons? how do Angels interact with their infrastructure generated covers?) would be good for clarifying any misinterpretations that people might have at current. <br /> <br /> Expanding out the range of Angelic Numina and lots of examples of angel antagonists. <br /> <br /> Thematic examination of the different roles Angels can play in a Demon game. From &quot;big bad&quot; to &quot;monster of the week&quot;. A look at possible non-antagonistic Angel's that Demons might choose to interact with for some reason. <br /> <br /> 2) Exiles - <br /> <br /> A deeper explanation of the Exile's state and how it is unique and interesting in its own right. <br /> <br /> How said state stands in relation to Demons and Angels. How they might relate to the God-Machine as both allies and enemies. <br /> <br /> Expanding out Exile archetypes and examples. Perhaps exile unique merits or abilities? <br /> <br /> 3) Cryptids -<br /> <br /> More of these monsters, fun examples, more traits and powers to use in constructing them.<br /> <br /> More discussion on how they come about. More info on cryptoflora and how it might be helpful as well as a hindrance to a Demon. <br /> <br /> Maybe some talk about Cryptids created from ghosts/spirits/extra dimensional beings? Previously mentioned as the possible basis for Rank 6+ Cryptids. <br /> <br /> 4) Crossover stuff -<br /> <br /> Not a lot of stuff here, but some useful stuff for cross-gameline storyhooks. Some basic discussion on how the God-Machine might interact other &quot;player&quot; supernaturals and the other &quot;big-bads&quot; of the NWoD such as the Strix, Genty, Abyss and Exarchs.<br /> <br /> General crossover rules for template vs template interact e.g. does demon blood give Vampires and odd effect if they drink it? Can Demons be blood-bonded? Are demons effected by Disquiet? etc. <br /> <br /> 5) Hell -<br /> <br /> Is their a cannon version? Is their a myriad of different possible Hells (one for each Agenda)? Can multiple hells exist at once? Does each demon have the ability to have their own personal hell? A toolkit to create your own hells for different PC's and NPC's. <br /> <br /> 6) The Cypher -<br /> <br /> General advice on handling this from an ST perspective. More example embeds. More examples of Cypher creation. A little more discussion on their narrative use. More explanation about the &quot;gnostic koen&quot; learned at the end of the Cypher and how that can be used as a springboard for more interesting PC development and stories rather then an &quot;end&quot;. <br /> <br /> 7) Important NPC Demons - <br /> <br /> Not the &quot;signature characters&quot; of the OWoD game lines, but the notable characters of the gameline e.g. Verney for Promethean, Count F***ing Dracula for Requiem. Satan has been mentioned already. Would love to have Lucifer be a different Demon (sometimes they work together). Ms Book from the various stories and examples in the books would also be awesome to see. <br /> <br /> 8) Meta-Stuff - <br /> <br /> Some options for the &quot;behind the curtain&quot; questions. Such as why has the God-Machine not solved the &quot;Angel's keep falling&quot; problem? What's up with the Cypher? Discussion on the idea of God-Machine and demiurge? The Satan Signal? Options for a historical myth e.g. the War in Heaven and such. <br /> <br /> Also it might just be me, but I would like another look at the Celebrants from the Core God-Machine book within the Demon framework? They seem to embody the opposite of the God-Machine, but they don't strike me as the sort of beings that most Unchained would get along with either. Good option maybe for another type of Antagonist? This last one might fall under the Hell and Crossover stuff as well I guess. <br /> <br /> That's all for now. Until other ideas strike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T08:26:39-07:00","id":196818,"title":"","content":"I'd be mildly amused if the Satan Signal came to be the new God-Machine.<br /> <br /> You know, like the G-M before GMC came out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T12:36:46-07:00","id":197101,"title":"","content":"I'm a big fan of the Tempter version of Hell. Subvert a lot of infrastructure, Rip the Gates into other worlds, and then move in. The Infrastructure provides the aether needed for comfort and defense, and there are many realms that exist sans god-machine. <br /> <br /> The thing is, Hell should be precarious. Just because God doesn't know where you are right now, doesn't mean he can't find your little home away from home. The same could be said for other Agendas' versions of Hell. An Agency of Saboteurs might (implausibly) wipe out every occult matrix, every facility, and smash the final C&amp;C Infrastructure. What then? What levels of survival can the God-Machine accommodate? Does the Demiurge have failsafes hidden in the Shadow or the Astral or...even the Supernal - symbols of technology and angelic myth that persist beyond destruction in the material plane?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T13:20:11-07:00","id":197128,"title":"","content":"It's not the Tempter's Hell if the God-Machine can get in. Hell is a place completely separate to the G-M and comfortable to demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T14:38:45-07:00","id":197172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/190544-wishlist-for-the-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=197128#post197128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not the Tempter's Hell if the God-Machine can get in. Hell is a place completely separate to the G-M and comfortable to demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should rephrase. Hell is an ideal state. Ideal states are hard (not impossible) to achieve. For my games, I want the establishment of a miltonesque Pandemonium to be fraught with uncertainty and paranoia. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T21:23:39-07:00","id":199640,"title":"","content":"Infrastructure: Specifically, what can you do with it once you've subverted it.<br /> <br /> The DtD gives:<br /> Harvesting Aether (boring but practical)<br /> Angeljacking (Situational useful, but only rewarding to one character at a time)<br /> Repairing Glitches (Useful, but could be boring if its used too often as a story device)<br /> GMC gives: going back in time<br /> Heirs gives going into an infrstructure to erase the G-M's knowledge of yourself or your family, which is a pretty compelling plot device.<br /> <br /> Give us ways to make raiding infrastructure something our players <i>want</i> to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T21:30:34-07:00","id":199650,"title":"","content":"Flowers gives you ways to make Infrastructure do what it does for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T22:38:33-07:00","id":199696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/190544-wishlist-for-the-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=197101#post197101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a big fan of the Tempter version of Hell. Subvert a lot of infrastructure, Rip the Gates into other worlds, and then move in. The Infrastructure provides the aether needed for comfort and defense, and there are many realms that exist sans god-machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Evil thought of the hour: A demon encounters a piece of the Prince of 10,000 leaves and decides to use it to make his/her personal hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 07-17-2014, 01:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T01:30:49-07:00","id":199796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/190544-wishlist-for-the-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=199696#post199696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Evil thought of the hour: A demon encounters a piece of the Prince of 10,000 leaves and decides to use it to make his/her personal hell.</div> </div> </div> </div> In my head canon, the prince is a god-organism seeking to usurp the god-machine, so that would be jumping into the fire to escape the frying pan.<br /> <br /> Now that archmage scelestus, the one who wants to make the world a paradise and thinks the abyss is the only way to achieve that, he'd make an interesting NPC in a demon game. Are the demons willing to risk destroying the world to save it from the god-machine?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T03:02:10-07:00","id":223990,"title":"","content":"I *really* want some 'endgame' stuff for demons, like the treatment given to the mages and changelings. If there is one splat that deserves some kind of possible high-end closure, it is Demon, i think.<br /> <br /> It would be nice to provide some merits, form bonuses and such at Primum 6+, as well as some endgame chronicles regarding the God Machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T17:45:24-07:00","id":233515,"title":"","content":"Something very relevent from the Gen Con panel; the Storyteller's Guide will have a chapter of alternate settings, one of which is &quot;a fantasy/psuedo-historical/Biblical setting.&quot; Another mentioned one was sci-fi future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:05:34-07:00","id":233540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/190544-wishlist-for-the-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=233515#post233515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something very relevent from the Gen Con panel; the Storyteller's Guide will have a chapter of alternate settings, one of which is &quot;a fantasy/psuedo-historical/Biblical setting.&quot; Another mentioned one was sci-fi future.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am so interested in all of this. Was there any word when the ST guide is coming out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T00:57:16-07:00","id":233954,"title":"","content":"That will be interesting, considering the thoroughly modern nature of demon as is. I wonder how hard it will be to gather aether without modern infrastructure, or if they're going to provide an alternate source....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T13:33:33-07:00","id":234588,"title":"","content":"Well, wheels were around in biblical times . . .actually, if you go back in time, technology gets really weird, like tempest prognosticators, which were barometers made from leeches, and then whatever the Baghdad Batteries did. . . .<br /> <br /> I'm surprised I hadn't thought of this before, but I suddenly want a steampunk Demon campaign *A*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T15:44:14-07:00","id":234737,"title":"","content":"While &quot;Biblical&quot; implies further back then I'd have thought, something during the Renaissance could very well work. Imagine the aqueducts of Rome as channels for Essence/Aether and then steal from Da Vinci for the Infrastructure that it powers. Bonus points for Assassin's Creed-style bullshitting things a little in the name of fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}